1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:02,315
There are thousands
of grains.

2
00:00:02,355 --> 00:00:04,080
So why
not ‘many rice’?

3
00:00:04,603 --> 00:00:06,777
Zoom in and you
see grains.

4
00:00:06,817 --> 00:00:08,176
But when I say
rice as food,

5
00:00:08,216 --> 00:00:09,655
I mean the amount
in the bowl,

6
00:00:09,695 --> 00:00:11,409
not a list
of grains.

7
00:00:11,937 --> 00:00:12,294
So:

8
00:00:12,334 --> 00:00:14,108
‘I ate too much
rice for lunch.’

9
00:00:14,148 --> 00:00:15,599
Not ‘too many rice’.

10
00:00:16,537 --> 00:00:17,430
Want to count?

11
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:18,404
Choose a unit:

12
00:00:18,444 --> 00:00:19,627
‘many grains
of rice’,

13
00:00:19,667 --> 00:00:20,987
‘two bowls of rice’.

14
00:00:21,027 --> 00:00:23,439
The number goes onto
grains or bowls.

15
00:00:24,170 --> 00:00:25,601
Bread works
the same way:

16
00:00:25,641 --> 00:00:27,404
‘three slices
of bread’.

17
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:28,284
Picture the amount,

18
00:00:28,324 --> 00:00:29,824
then pick the unit.

